To be more concrete, don't eat kobolds, mummies, zombies, killer bees.
Generally no food that was lying aroung too long (as a rule of thumb:
not older than 50 moves).  Don't eat corpses of you own race.  Don't
eat corpses of your pet.

You can eat 'd', 'f', 'G', 'o', 'h', 'q', ':', 'e' (but see below).
(I forgot, if you play non-tty you don't know what the letters mean?
dog-like, cat-like, gnomes, orcs, dwarfs, rothes, newts, eyes.)
There are much more monsters that you can eat, but you will meet them
later in te game.  The listed monster classes are the monsters that
you might meet early in the game.

> > What are the common death causes for your games ?

Being hit by a death ray, for example.  :-)

But the death causes for beginners differ...

As a beginner you might hit floating eyes, which is a Bad Thing.
Being sorrounded by monster hordes is a Bad Thing - avoid that.
You will find it a bad idea eating while satiated.
Leave those fountains alone - don't drink!
Not retreating while low at hit points is unwise.
Being overloaded should be avoided.

